# Parameters and Return Values

Parameters and return values are both used to pass information to and from methods.

Parameters are variables that are passed into methods.

Return values are the values that are returned from methods.

```java
public class ParametersAndReturnValues {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int x = 10;
        int y = 20;
        int z = add(x, y);
        System.out.println(z);
    }

    public static int add(int x, int y) {
        return x + y;
    }
}
```

